{"When organization.features.includes('use-table-widget-visualization') is true, TableWidgetVisualization receives hardcoded empty values (columns: [], data: []) instead of the actual result.data and result.meta from the query, causing the table to render with no rows and no columns regardless of what data is available.": 0.993133008480072, "The analytics.record('preprod_artifact.api.assemble', ...) call executes before the feature flag check, so analytics events are recorded even when the feature is disabled and the endpoint returns 404. The event name implies a successful assembly operation, but the request was rejected.": 0.9779626727104187, "When transparentMask is true, RightMask uses transparent which equals rgba(0, 0, 0, 0), causing the gradient to interpolate through black on dark mode backgrounds and producing visible color banding. LeftMask correctly uses Color(p.theme.background).alpha(0).rgb().string() but RightMask should match that pattern.": 0.963380753993988, "When tableData is nullish at runtime, line 94 throws TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object because Object.keys(tableData?.meta.fields) evaluates to Object.keys(undefined). This is inconsistent with the defensive handling on line 103 (tableData?.data ?? []). Should add optional chaining and a fallback: Object.keys(tableData?.meta?.fields ?? {}).": 0.9815278053283691, "The comment on lines 19-20 states top events are only supported when there are no multiple y-axes, but the diff removed the visualizes.some(visualize => visualize.yAxes.length > 1) check. The function now returns TOP_EVENTS_LIMIT even with multiple y-axes, which contradicts the documented constraint.": 0.4681570529937744}